Run the script once yourself, in a PowerShell session with the ActiveDirectory module and an account that may create users. The account is the bait, not the file, and nobody learns its password: the script generates it and does not keep it. The account holds no rights and belongs to no group beyond the default. Then move the account to the organizational unit of your administrator accounts and keep the script where the documentation of the directory is, if you want it to be found. The script raises no event on its own; only an attempt to sign in as `{{.Persona.AdminAccount}}` does, and only on a domain controller whose log you forward.
